msgid "Some history"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After having migrated the whole Quarkus code base and Quarkiverse extensions "
"to @ConfigMapping interfaces in Quarkus 3.19,\n"
"we announce the sunsetting of legacy config classes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In 2022, we introduced in Quarkus a new configuration infrastructure for "
"extensions based on interfaces annotated with `@ConfigMapping`.\n"
"They were a replacement for the legacy config classes that were used in "
"Quarkus extensions,\n"
"which came with several issues and were specific to extensions (you couldn't "
"use them in applications)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The new `@ConfigMapping` infrastructure unified extension and application "
"configuration on the same infrastructure."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In Quarkus 3.19k, released late February this year, we moved all the core "
"extensions to this new infrastructure (except for some classes that were "
"kept for compatibility purposes)\n"
"and deprecated the legacy config classes support, together with dropping "
"close to all the existing config classes: we kept a few for compatibility "
"reasons."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension annotation processor was also modified to require a specific "
"option `-AlegacyConfigRoot=true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The plan has always been to sunset the legacy config classes so that we "
"could remove all the machinery related to it,\n"
"and offer a single unified configuration mechanism."
msgstr ""

msgid "Current state"
msgstr ""

msgid "The current state of the public Quarkus ecosystem is the following:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All the Core extensions are using the new ``@ConfigMapping``-based "
"infrastructure."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All the Quarkiverse extensions have been updated to use the new "
"``@ConfigMapping``-based infrastructure (except for `quarkus-logging-json` "
"but we have a https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-logging-json/pull/"
"345[pull request ready])."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some other extensions participating to the Ecosystem CI have also been "
"updated such as https://persistence.blazebit.com/[Blaze-Persistence]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We know some of you also develop custom extensions so we highly recommend "
"moving your custom extensions to `@ConfigMapping` as soon as possible, if "
"not already done."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find more information about it in https://quarkus.io/guides/writing-"
"extensions#configuration[our documentation] and a ton of examples in the "
"https://github.com/search?q="
"repo%3Aquarkusio%2Fquarkus%20%40ConfigMapping&type=code[Quarkus Core "
"repository] or the https://github.com/search?q="
"org%3Aquarkiverse+%40ConfigMapping&type=code[Quarkiverse extensions]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you have any questions while migrating, please ask them in https://github."
"com/quarkusio/quarkus/discussions/categories/q-a[GitHub Discussions], we "
"will be happy to help."
msgstr ""

msgid "Coming in 3.25"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In 3.25, we will throw an error when the extension annotation processor is "
"used with `-AlegacyConfigRoot=true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**It won't be possible to build an extension containing legacy config "
"classes with Quarkus 3.25 anymore.**"
msgstr ""

msgid "Coming in 3.26"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In 3.26, we will remove all support for legacy config classes, meaning they "
"won't work anymore.\n"
"**If one of the extensions of your application is using any legacy config "
"class, your application won't build.**"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that since 3.19.4, you get a warning if any of the extensions in your "
"application is using legacy config classes."
msgstr ""

msgid "We will also drop all the compatibility classes we kept until then:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`GlobalDevServicesConfig`: use `DevServicesConfig` instead"
msgstr ""

msgid "`HttpConfiguration`: use `VertxHttpConfig` instead"
msgstr ""

msgid "`HttpBuildTimeConfig`: use `VertxHttpBuildTimeConfig` instead"
msgstr ""

msgid "Feedback and questions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you have any feedback or questions regarding this change, please either "
"use https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/discussions/categories/q-a[GitHub "
"Discussions] or the https://groups.google.com/g/quarkus-dev[quarkus-dev "
"Google groups]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
